// Package tmplrt is support for code generated by rastrillo generate. It
// is not for app code: write templates with html/template and let the
// generator call into this package.
//
// A compiled template has to produce the same bytes as html/template
// does. html/template picks an escaper chain for each {{action}} when it
// first executes, and its escaper functions are not exported. This
// package holds Rastrillo's own copies of all sixteen, and of
// _eval_args_, the argument formatter escaping puts in front of
// {{html .X}}, with the same names html/template registers in Escapers,
// so generated code can call them directly and a test can run them
// against the real thing.
//
// The generic escapers (HTMLEscaper and friends) take the same
// arguments as the originals and behave the same for every input:
// untyped nil, typed content such as template.HTML, Stringers, errors
// and pointers. The *String functions in fast.go are for a value whose
// static type is exactly string. They skip the type inspection and do
// not allocate when the input needs no escaping.
//
// The rest is text/template's evaluation, which html/template runs
// underneath: its builtins (builtins.go), and what it does with a value
// that compiled code cannot know until the data arrives (dynamic.go):
// look up a field, method or map key; convert an argument to a
// parameter type; range over whatever the value is. Both are ported
// from text/template in Go 1.26.10, over reflect.Value as there, with
// its checks, their order and its errors.
//
// The escapers are ported from html/template in Go 1.26.10. Only the
// names are exported; the code is otherwise unchanged. The state machine
// that stripTags uses to walk HTML lives in internal/htmlctx, with
// the CSS and JS helpers it shares with the escapers, because the
// escaping pass in internal/tmplescape walks the same one. Content
// types are html/template's own (template.HTML and so on), so a value
// that app code builds for html/template is recognised here too.
//
// The ported files carry the Go authors' copyright notice and are used
// under their BSD licence, reproduced in LICENSE-go in this directory.
package tmplrt
